1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
After the rain stops, where does every drop go next?

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Some water follows gravity across the ground.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
That moving water is called surface runoff.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Hard surfaces usually let less water soak into the ground.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Some runoff enters drains, streams, and rivers.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Other drops land where the ground can welcome them.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
This is infiltration: water soaking into soil and rock.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Plants can use some of that water, and return part of it to the air.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
One storm can send different drops along very different paths.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Soil, plants, slopes, and pavement all change the journey.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The next time rain ends, look closely. The journey is still happening.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Every drop has a path. And every path is part of a larger cycle.
